    <Element Type="Comment" Id="250D0FA9">
        <Comment>
            Attack wave format:
                Wait X seconds
                If (AI player can attack) Then
                    Wait Y seconds
                    Send attack wave, arriving in Z seconds
                End
            - Once an AI is crippled, his attack wave turns get skipped, allowing the other AIs to step in and continue hitting the player.
            - The &quot;X&quot; wait occurs even if the AI is crippled, giving the player a little extra time between waves for every AI he kills.
            - The &quot;Y&quot; wait is really part of the attack wave; its purpose is just to delay the wave&apos;s preparation (and therefore its gathering).
            - The &quot;Z&quot; wait is the standard prep and send time of the wave.
            - If the AI is alive, the wave will be sent in (X+Y+Z) time.  Otherwise, we wait X seconds and then try the next AI.
        </Comment>
    </Element>
